IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-reviews`

-- Tests for Regulations ss 17 to 19 and 31, with the working beside each assertion. Dates
-- are counted by hand: the 180 days are the 180 days after the day of the notice.

§ `Regulations s 17 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the Minister may amend or rescind the decision` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may amend or rescind the decision` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister may amend or rescind the decision` FALSE TRUE

§ `Regulations s 18 -- tests`

-- A request, varied by the decision it is about and whether the person is dissatisfied.
GIVEN decision IS A `Decision of the Minister`
      dissatisfied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Request for reconsideration`
`a request about` decision `whose maker is dissatisfied:` dissatisfied MEANS
    `Request for reconsideration` WITH
        `the decision` IS decision
        `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS dissatisfied
        `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
        `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
        `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
        `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
        `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
        `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
        `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

-- The kinds of decision that s 18(1) and (2) cover, and the ones they do not.
#ASSERT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `a decision respecting the amount of a benefit that the person has received or will receive` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `a decision imposing a penalty under section 35` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `a decision on a request for reconsideration made under subsection 18(4)` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `a decision on a request for an extension of time made under subsection 19(4)` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `any other decision` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)
-- A person who is not dissatisfied has nothing to ask.
#ASSERT NOT `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` (`a request about` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` FALSE)

-- The 180 days, counted by hand.
-- 1 January 2026: January ends at day 30, February at 58, March at 89, April at 119, May at 150, June at 180 = 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 30
-- 31 August 2025: 30 September (30), 31 October (61), 30 November (91), 31 December (122), 31 January (153), 27 February 2026 (180).
#ASSERT `the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` (YMD 2025 8 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27
-- 1 January 2028 (a leap year): January ends at 30, February at 59, March at 90, April at 120, May at 151, 29 June at 180.
#ASSERT `the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` (YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2028 6 29

-- In time: on the last day, and a day later; with an extension to 15 September 2026.
`a request made on 30 June 2026` MEANS `a request about` `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE

`a request made on 1 July 2026` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 7 1
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

`a request made on 15 September 2026 after an extension to that day` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 9 15
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS JUST (YMD 2026 9 15)
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

`a request made on 16 September 2026 after an extension to 15 September` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 9 16
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS JUST (YMD 2026 9 15)
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the request was made in time` `a request made on 30 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the request was made in time` `a request made on 1 July 2026`
#ASSERT `the request was made in time` `a request made on 15 September 2026 after an extension to that day`
#ASSERT NOT `the request was made in time` `a request made on 16 September 2026 after an extension to 15 September`

-- 18(3): each content requirement on its own. (b) binds only when the person is incapable.
`a request that is not in writing` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

`a request without the person's name, address and number` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS FALSE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

`a request for an incapable person without the representative's details` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

`a request for an incapable person with the representative's details` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS TRUE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

`a request that does not identify the decision or the reasons` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
    `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
    `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
    `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
    `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
    `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
    `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
    `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
    `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `a request made on 30 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `a request that is not in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `a request without the person's name, address and number`
#ASSERT NOT `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `a request for an incapable person without the representative's details`
#ASSERT `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `a request for an incapable person with the representative's details`
#ASSERT NOT `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `a request that does not identify the decision or the reasons`

-- 18(4): the Minister's duty arises only for a proper request, in time, about a covered decision.
#ASSERT `the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` `a request made on 30 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` `a request made on 1 July 2026`
#ASSERT `the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` `a request made on 15 September 2026 after an extension to that day`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` `a request that is not in writing`
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` (`a request about` `any other decision` `whose maker is dissatisfied:` TRUE)

§ `Regulations s 19 -- tests`

-- 19(1): 185 days after the end of the 180 days. 180 days end 30 June 2026; July (31) to
-- December (31) is 184 days to 31 December 2026, so the 185th is 1 January 2027.
#ASSERT `the last day to ask the Minister to extend the 180 days` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT `the request for an extension was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the request for an extension was made in time` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 2)
-- 19(3): each situation, with and without the Minister's satisfaction; "none of these" never.
#ASSERT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `an emergency, if a state of emergency has been declared by a federal or provincial minister under federal or provincial law` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `a natural or human-made disaster, such as a flood or fire` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `a civil disturbance, such as a riot` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `a disruption in public services, such as a strike` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `a serious accident, injury or illness suffered by the person` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `an emotional or mental distress suffered by the person, such as from a death in their family` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `a natural or human-made disaster, such as a flood or fire` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `none of these` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `none of these` FALSE
-- 19(2) and 19(4): the form and manner, and in time.
#ASSERT `the Minister must consider the request for an extension and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reason` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must consider the request for an extension and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reason` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2027 1 2) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must consider the request for an extension and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reason` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 9 1) FALSE

§ `Regulations s 31 -- tests`

#ASSERT `the Minister must take remedial action to put the person in the position they would be in` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must take remedial action to put the person in the position they would be in` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must take remedial action to put the person in the position they would be in` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Minister must take remedial action to put the person in the position they would be in` TRUE TRUE FALSE
